@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 [&_h2]:text-secondary [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:mt-6 [&_p]:text-base-content/80">
<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary mb-2">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    This page summarizes what account and cookie data Swords and Ravens stores
    about you, and how you can request it be removed.
</p>

<h2>Account data</h2>
<p>
    When you register, or sign in via Google, Discord, or Facebook, we store your username,
    e-mail address (if provided by the sign-in method), and gameplay-related settings and
    statistics (game history, win rate). If you sign in with an external provider, we never see or
    store your password on that provider — only the profile fields it explicitly shares with us.
</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>
    We use a session/authentication cookie to keep you signed in; this cookie is essential and is
    set as soon as you sign in, independent of the consent banner. We do not use analytics or
    advertising cookies of our own. If you sign in via an external OAuth provider, that provider
    may set its own cookies during the redirect — see their respective privacy policies.
</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>
    You can review and update your profile settings from your account page at any time. To request
    a full export or deletion of your account data, contact the site operator.
</p>
</div>
